WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.257 --> 00:00:18.839
Rachel Lynde lived on the main road in Avonlea, a town on Prince Edward Island, off the coast

2
00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:19.419
of Canada.

3
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:25.282
Anybody who was coming to or leaving Avonlea had to use the main road and pass by the

4
00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:26.042
Lyndes' house.

5
00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:29.844
Mrs. Lynde was always watching from her kitchen window.

6
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.023
Mrs. Lynde sat at her window one afternoon in early June.

7
00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:39.047
At half-past three, Matthew Cuthbert was driving his buggy down the road.

8
00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:41.129
He wore his best suit.

9
00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:45.092
"Matthew should be planting turnip seeds now like Mr.

10
00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:46.413
Lynde," thought Mrs.

11
00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:51.257
Lynde. "But instead he is in his buggy and dressed in his best suit!

12
00:00:51.937 --> 00:00:54.840
Where is Matthew Cuthbert going and why?"

13
00:00:55.824 --> 00:00:58.546
If it was any other man in Avonlea, Mrs.

14
00:00:58.586 --> 00:01:01.067
Lynde might be able to guess where he was going.

15
00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:06.270
But Matthew Cuthbert so rarely left home that it had to be something unusual.

16
00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.653
He was the shyest man alive and hated to go anywhere he might have to talk.

17
00:01:12.473 --> 00:01:17.956
"I'll just go to Green Gables and ask his sister, Marilla, where he's gone," she decided.

18
00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:21.278
After hearing "Come in!"

19
00:01:21.658 --> 00:01:23.179
from Marilla, Mrs.

20
00:01:23.239 --> 00:01:24.740
Lynde stepped into the kitchen.

21
00:01:25.564 --> 00:01:27.986
She looked carefully at everything on the table.

22
00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:33.931
There were three plates, so Marilla must have been expecting a visitor to come home with Matthew.

23
00:01:34.571 --> 00:01:40.456
But the dishes were everyday dishes and the cake was plain, so the expected visitor could not be

24
00:01:40.556 --> 00:01:41.917
anybody too important.

25
00:01:41.937 --> 00:01:45.560
"Good evening, Rachel," Marilla greeted Mrs.

26
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.122
Lynde. "This is a lovely evening, isn't it?

27
00:01:48.703 --> 00:01:49.604
Won't you sit down?

28
00:01:50.124 --> 00:01:50.785
How are you?"

29
00:01:51.405 --> 00:01:52.886
Marilla was tall and thin.

30
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:56.525
Even though she looked stern, she did have a sense of humor.

31
00:01:56.545 --> 00:01:58.767
"We're well," said Mrs.

32
00:01:58.847 --> 00:02:04.250
Lynde. "Though I thought you weren't well when I saw Matthew in the buggy today."

33
00:02:05.151 --> 00:02:06.852
Marilla had expected Mrs.

34
00:02:06.932 --> 00:02:08.513
Lynde to visit because Mrs.

35
00:02:08.573 --> 00:02:10.194
Lynde was a curious person.

36
00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:13.537
"Matthew went to Bright River," Marilla said.

37
00:02:13.557 --> 00:02:18.240
"We're getting a little boy from an orphanage, and he's coming on the train tonight."

38
00:02:19.044 --> 00:02:23.945
If Marilla had said that Matthew had gone to meet a kangaroo from Australia, Mrs.

39
00:02:24.005 --> 00:02:25.986
Lynde could not be more surprised.

40
00:02:26.566 --> 00:02:29.127
She actually stopped talking for five seconds.

41
00:02:29.147 --> 00:02:32.308
"Why on earth would you do that?"

42
00:02:32.728 --> 00:02:34.028
she asked disapprovingly.

43
00:02:34.048 --> 00:02:39.570
"We've been thinking about it for some time—all winter, in fact," replied Marilla.

44
00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.530
"Matthew is growing older.

45
00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.951
He's sixty, and his heart is not so good.

46
00:02:45.551 --> 00:02:47.892
It's difficult to hire someone to do farm work."

47
00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.010
Mrs. Lynde always said what she thought.

48
00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:57.034
In this case it was, "Well, Marilla, I think you're doing a very foolish thing.

49
00:02:57.854 --> 00:03:01.817
You're bringing a strange child into your house and you don't know a thing about him!

50
00:03:02.478 --> 00:03:08.001
Last week in the newspaper, it said that a family took an orphan boy and he set fire

51
00:03:08.061 --> 00:03:12.765
to the house at night— on purpose, Marilla—and nearly burnt them in their beds."

52
00:03:13.565 --> 00:03:15.827
Marilla was neither offended nor alarmed.

53
00:03:16.647 --> 00:03:21.490
Meanwhile Matthew Cuthbert and the horse jogged the ten kilometers to the station.

54
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:27.072
It was a pretty road, and the air was sweet with the smell of apple and plum blossoms.

55
00:03:27.972 --> 00:03:31.674
When Matthew arrived, there was no train, and he thought he was early.

56
00:03:32.314 --> 00:03:36.876
The long platform was almost deserted, except for a girl sitting at the end.

57
00:03:37.596 --> 00:03:40.217
Matthew walked quickly past her to the station office.

58
00:03:40.237 --> 00:03:47.524
"The five-thirty train has gone, but there was a passenger for you, a little girl," said the stationmaster.

59
00:03:47.544 --> 00:03:50.507
"I'm not expecting a girl," said Matthew, surprised.

60
00:03:50.527 --> 00:03:52.228
"It's a boy I've come for."

61
00:03:52.829 --> 00:03:54.911
The stationmaster raised his eyebrows.

62
00:03:54.931 --> 00:03:57.253
"Well, I guess there's some mistake.

63
00:03:57.773 --> 00:03:59.895
Mrs. Spencer came off the train with that girl.

64
00:04:00.456 --> 00:04:03.738
She said you and your sister, Marilla, were adopting the girl from an orphanage."

65
00:04:04.619 --> 00:04:06.141
The girl watched Matthew.

66
00:04:06.761 --> 00:04:11.285
She was eleven years old and dressed in a very old and very ugly dress.

67
00:04:12.046 --> 00:04:14.248
On her head was a worn-out, brown hat.

68
00:04:14.992 --> 00:04:19.115
Under the hat were two braids of very thick, very red hair.

69
00:04:19.875 --> 00:04:24.118
Her face was small, white, and thin, and she had many freckles.

70
00:04:24.138 --> 00:04:26.660
"I suppose you are Mr.

71
00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.042
Matthew Cuthbert of Green Gables?"

72
00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.483
she said in a clear, sweet voice.

73
00:04:32.664 --> 00:04:33.845
She held out her hand.

74
00:04:33.865 --> 00:04:35.946
"I'm very glad to see you.

75
00:04:35.966 --> 00:04:38.348
I was afraid you weren't coming for me.

76
00:04:38.948 --> 00:04:44.012
I had decided if you didn't come for me, I'd climb up that big wild cherry tree.

77
00:04:44.676 --> 00:04:48.819
It would be lovely to sleep in a wild cherry tree under the moon, don't you think?"

78
00:04:50.219 --> 00:04:54.001
Matthew shook the little hand awkwardly and wondered what to say.

79
00:04:54.682 --> 00:05:00.045
Matthew could not say there was a mistake; he would take her home and let Marilla explain everything.

80
00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:03.027
"I'm sorry I was late," he said shyly.

81
00:05:03.047 --> 00:05:04.087
"Come along.

82
00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:05.728
The horse is over in the yard."

83
00:05:05.748 --> 00:05:11.451
"Oh, I'm very glad you came," the girl said, "even if it would be nice to sleep in

84
00:05:11.491 --> 00:05:12.152
a cherry tree.

85
00:05:12.904 --> 00:05:15.726
It's wonderful I'm going to live with you and belong to you.

86
00:05:15.746 --> 00:05:19.047
I've never belonged to anybody—not really."

87
00:05:19.668 --> 00:05:22.569
The girl kept talking as they drove down the main road.

88
00:05:22.589 --> 00:05:24.310
"Isn't it beautiful?"

89
00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:25.271
she said.

90
00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:30.534
"I've always heard that Prince Edward Island is the prettiest place in the world.

91
00:05:31.114 --> 00:05:35.036
I used to imagine living here, but I never expected I actually would.

92
00:05:35.456 --> 00:05:36.677
Am I talking too much?"

93
00:05:37.197 --> 00:05:37.878
she went on.

94
00:05:37.898 --> 00:05:40.059
"People always tell me I do.

95
00:05:40.619 --> 00:05:42.080
If you say so, I'll stop.

96
00:05:42.632 --> 00:05:45.054
I can stop, though it is difficult."

97
00:05:45.854 --> 00:05:48.756
Surprisingly, Matthew was enjoying himself.

98
00:05:49.397 --> 00:05:52.359
He'd never expected to enjoy the company of a young girl.

99
00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.502
He said shyly, "Oh, you can talk as much as you like.

100
00:05:57.062 --> 00:05:57.542
I don't mind."

101
00:05:57.562 --> 00:05:59.424
"I'm so glad.

102
00:05:59.944 --> 00:06:01.785
You and I will get along just fine.

103
00:06:02.386 --> 00:06:04.587
I feel nearly perfectly happy.

104
00:06:04.607 --> 00:06:08.910
I can't feel perfectly happy because—well, what color is this?"

105
00:06:09.711 --> 00:06:11.532
The girl held up one of her braids.

106
00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:13.425
"It's red, isn't it?"

107
00:06:13.785 --> 00:06:14.245
he said.

108
00:06:14.265 --> 00:06:18.767
"Yes, it's red," she said, sighing.

109
00:06:18.787 --> 00:06:22.028
"Now you see why I can't be perfectly happy.

110
00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.049
Nobody with red hair can be perfectly happy."

111
00:06:25.069 --> 00:06:28.511
"We're near home now," Matthew said uneasily.

112
00:06:29.291 --> 00:06:34.613
As they approached Green Gables, he did not think about Marilla or himself or the mistake.

113
00:06:35.353 --> 00:06:39.395
He thought only about the child's disappointment when she discovered the truth.
